{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexRogersDilog","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleSumRule","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm"],"declarations":138,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds","kind":"theorem","line":1925,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1925-L1945","doc":"**`FiveTwoSaddleSumRule`, instantiated.**\n\n`QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.FiveTwoSaddleSumRule` is declared there as a class with no\ninstance, with the comment \"No instance is provided: the statement is open\".\nHere is the instance, for `Li = cLiTwoExt`, `y = (y₁, y₂, y₃)` the three roots of\nthe saddle cubic, and `b = (−1, +1, +1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_sum_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_sum_V","kind":"theorem","line":1884,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1884-L1923","doc":"**The corpus's own conjecture, proved.**\n\n`QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.FiveTwoSaddleSumRule` is stated there as a class with no\ninstance — \"numerically verified, not proved\". With `Vⱼ = 3·Li₂(yⱼ) +\n(log yⱼ + bⱼπi)²` and `b = (−1, +1, +1)` on `(y₁, y₂, y₃)`,\n\n    Σⱼ Vⱼ = −3π²/2 + 2π·log(y₃)·i\n\nso `Σⱼ Re Vⱼ = −3π²/2`, which is the class's field. Both halves are elementary,\nas the lane's probes measured — the real part is the conjecture, the imaginary\npart `2π·log y₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule","kind":"theorem","line":1850,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1850-L1882","doc":"**The 5₂ saddle sum rule.**\n\nThere are three roots of `X³ − 2X² + 3X − 1` — one real in `(0,1)` and a\nconjugate pair — and\n\n    Σ Li₂(yⱼ) = −π²/6 − ½·log²y₃ + (2/3)·(arg y₁ − π)²\n\nwith `Li₂` the corpus's integral continuation `cLiTwoExt`, which agrees with the\nprincipal branch off `[1,∞)`. This is the quantity the lane calls `A`, and the\nright side is the expression the corpus records as the sum rule's target.\n\nThe chain: the complex five-term identity (Route 54) at `(y₃, y₁)` and\n`(y₃, y₂)`; the anharmonic evaluations (59, 60, 62, 63); the branch equations\nfrom `y² = (1−y)³` (65); the root data (66–68); and the logarithm evaluations\n(69). Every step is sorry-free with the standard axioms. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:fivetwo-saddle-sum-rule","label":"prop:fivetwo-saddle-sum-rule","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/fivetwo-saddle-sum-rule.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.sum_cLiTwoExt_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.sum_cLiTwoExt_closed","kind":"theorem","line":1814,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1814-L1842","doc":"**The sum rule's stated form, from the root data.**\n\n    Σ Li₂ = −π²/6 − ½·log²t + (2/3)·(arg a − π)²\n\nEvery logarithm in Route 68's capstone has been evaluated: `log a`, `log b` from\nthe modulus relation `‖a‖²·t = 1`, and `log A₃`, `log B₃` from Route 61's angle\nidentity. What is left is `π²`, `log t` and `arg a`.\n\nThis is the sum rule's **shape**, reached from `SaddleRoots` — a structure whose\nfields are facts about the cubic. On its own it would say nothing about the\nactual 5₂ saddle sum `A`; that needs `SaddleRoots` to be inhabited by the actual\nroots, which `SaddleRoots.ofRealRoot` and `instance : Nonempty SaddleRoots`\nestablish (below, from the intermediate value theorem and an explicit square\nroot). `fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule` is this theorem with that instance supplied.\n\n**The 5₂ sum rule is PROVED**:\n`QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule`\nand `fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds`, sorry-free, standard axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.sum_cLiTwoExt_root_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.sum_cLiTwoExt_root_data","kind":"theorem","line":1780,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1780-L1812","doc":"**Route 64's capstone, with every hypothesis discharged from the root data.**\n\n    2·Σ Li₂ = 2π²/3 − (iπ/2)(log A₃ − log B₃ + log b − log a)\n              − (2/3)·Σ log² + (2πi/3)·Σ εⱼ·log yⱼ\n\nThe pentagon values are `pentagon_upper` / `pentagon_lower`, the imaginary-part\nconditions are `A3_im_pos` / `B3_im_neg`, and the three branch equations are\n`branch_upper` / `branch_lower` / `branch_real` — all theorems about\n`SaddleRoots`. **Nothing is assumed beyond the structure.**\n\n⚠ The right side is still logarithms, not `−π²/6 − ½log²t + (2/3)(θ−π)²`. Turning\nit into that needs `arg A₃ = (π − arg a)/3` (`saddle_clog_cube_of_roots`, proved\nfrom root data) and `log a = −½log t + i·arg a` (`normSq_mul`, proved, plus the\nargument). Those substitutions are not made here.\n\n**The 5₂ sum rule is PROVED**: `FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule`\nand `fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds`, sorry-free, standard axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_cLiTwoExt_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_cLiTwoExt_eval","kind":"theorem","line":1739,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1739-L1778","doc":"**Route 58's chain, end to end.**\n\n    2·Σ Li₂(yⱼ) = 2π²/3 − (iπ/2)·(log A₃ − log B₃ + log b − log a)\n                  − (2/3)·Σ log²yⱼ + (2πi/3)·Σ εⱼ·log yⱼ\n\nThe left side is twice the sum rule's `A`. The right side has **no dilogarithm in\nit at all** — only `π²` and logarithms of the roots. Everything on the way here is\nproved: the two pentagon instances are `pentagonSum_eq_pi_sq_div_two`, the four\nevaluations are the one-log forms, and the bridge is the branch equations.\n\n⚠ The inputs that remain are the two pentagon values (theorems), the branch\nequations (`hε`), and — to turn the right side into `−π²/6 − ½log²y₃ +\n(2/3)(θ−π)²` — the root-data facts `|y₁|²y₃ = 1`, `y₂ = conj y₁`, and\n`arg A₃ = (π − arg y₁)/3` (`saddle_clog_cube_of_roots`). None of the latter is\ndischarged here.\n\n**The 5₂ sum rule is PROVED**: `FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule`\nand `fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds`, sorry-free, standard axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_cLiTwoExt_of_branch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_cLiTwoExt_of_branch","kind":"theorem","line":1715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1715-L1737","doc":"**`A` from the orbit sum and the branch data**, with no dilogarithm on the\nright beyond the orbit sum itself:\n\n    2·Σ Li₂(yⱼ) = 2·Σ L(yⱼ) − (2/3)·Σ log²yⱼ + (2πi/3)·Σ εⱼ·log yⱼ\n\nCombined with `saddle_sum_cRogersL` this expresses `A` in **logarithms and `π²`\nalone** — which is Route 58's chain, end to end, modulo the branch equations\nthemselves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_cLiTwoExt_eq_sum_cRogersL_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_cLiTwoExt_eq_sum_cRogersL_sub","kind":"theorem","line":1705,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1705-L1713","doc":"`Σ Li₂ = Σ L − ½·Σ log·log`, by the definition of `cRogersL`. This is the\nwhole of the `Σ L` ↔ `A` conversion; the content is in evaluating the second sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_log_mul_log_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.sum_log_mul_log_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":1689,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1689-L1703","doc":"**The log·log sum, from three branch equations.**\n\n    Σ lⱼ·mⱼ = (2/3)·Σ lⱼ² − (2πi/3)·Σ εⱼ·lⱼ        given 2lⱼ − 3mⱼ = 2πi·εⱼ\n\n`lⱼ` stands for `log yⱼ` and `mⱼ` for `log(1−yⱼ)`. Nothing quadratic in `m`\nsurvives — that is the whole point, and it is why `A` inherits `Σ L`'s\nelementary shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_sum_cRogersL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_sum_cRogersL","kind":"theorem","line":1649,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1649-L1677","doc":"**The orbit sum, from two pentagon instances and the four one-log\nevaluations.**\n\n    2·(L(c) + L(a) + L(b)) = 2π²/3 − (iπ/2)·(log A₃ − log B₃ + log b − log a)\n\nWith `b = conj a`, `B₃ = conj A₃` and `c` real, the bracket is `2i·(arg A₃ −\narg a)` and this reads `Σ L = π²/3 + (π/2)(arg A₃ − arg a)`. Route 61's\n`saddle_clog_cube_of_roots` then supplies `arg A₃`, and Route 47's closed form\nfollows.\n\n⚠ The two pentagon values are hypotheses here. They are theorems —\n`pentagonSum_eq_pi_sq_div_two` — but stating them as inputs keeps this lemma pure\nbookkeeping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_one_sub_inv_sub_of_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_one_sub_inv_sub_of_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":1618,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1618-L1636","doc":"**The anharmonic relation above the real axis.** The mirror of\n`cRogersL_one_sub_inv_sub_of_im_neg`:\n\n    L(1 − 1/z) − L(z) = −π²/6 − (iπ/2)·log z      for `Im z > 0`\n\nWith the four one-log forms — inversion and the anharmonic step, each on both\nsides of the axis — the anharmonic group's action on `cRogersL` is completely\ntabulated, and every evaluation Route 58 needs is a substitution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_one_sub_inv_sub_of_im_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_one_sub_inv_sub_of_im_neg","kind":"theorem","line":1598,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1598-L1616","doc":"**The anharmonic relation, with the `log(−z)` eliminated.**\n\n    L(1 − 1/z) − L(z) = −π²/6 + (iπ/2)·log z          for `Im z < 0`\n\nAs with inversion, the `log²` terms cancel completely: below the real axis the\norder-3 anharmonic step costs `π²` plus `π` times a single logarithm. This is the\nform Route 58's link G4 uses — its value has no `log²` for the same reason G3's\ndoes not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.inv_mem_rogersDomain_of_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.inv_mem_rogersDomain_of_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1591,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1591-L1596","doc":"A point off the real axis has its inverse off both cuts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_one_sub_inv_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_one_sub_inv_sub","kind":"theorem","line":1573,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1573-L1589","doc":"**The anharmonic relation, evaluated.** Reflection at `1/z` minus inversion:\n\n    L(1 − 1/z) − L(z) = π²/3 + ½·log(−z)² − ½·log z·log(−z)\n\n`z ↦ 1 − 1/z` is the order-3 element of the anharmonic group, and Route 55 showed\nit carries the 5₂ saddle cubic onto `X³ − X + 1`. This is that map read on `L`,\nand it is the analytic content of Route 58's link G4 — what remains there is\nevaluating the two logarithms, i.e. branch pinning. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_add_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_add_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":1555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1555-L1571","doc":"**Complex Rogers reflection.** `L(z) + L(1−z) = π²/6` on all of\n`rogersDomain` — every `z` off both real cuts, no branch hypothesis.\n\nThe constant is pinned at `z = 1/2`, where `cRogersL_ofReal` and the corpus's\nreal `rogersL_reflection` give it outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_cRogersL_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_cRogersL_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":1539,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1539-L1553","doc":"**`L(z) + L(1−z)` has vanishing derivative** — identically, with no branch\ncondition. This is the Rogers normalisation's whole point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.one_sub_mem_rogersDomain_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.one_sub_mem_rogersDomain_iff","kind":"theorem","line":1525,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1525-L1537","doc":"`rogersDomain` is invariant under `z ↦ 1 − z`: the involution swaps the two\ncuts `(−∞,0]` and `[1,∞)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.instNonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.instNonempty","kind":"instance","line":1499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1499-L1501","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ofRealRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ofRealRoot","kind":"def","line":1459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1459-L1497","doc":"**From a real root, a `SaddleRoots`.** The conjugate pair is\n`(2−t)/2 ± i·√(3t²−4t+8)/2`, the roots of the residual quadratic\n`x² + (t−2)x + (t²−2t+3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.disc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.disc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":1455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1455-L1457","doc":"The discriminant of the residual quadratic is negative — unconditionally, not\njust on `(0,1)`: `3t² − 4t + 8` has discriminant `16 − 96 < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.exists_real_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.exists_real_root","kind":"theorem","line":1445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1445-L1453","doc":"The saddle cubic has a real root in `(0,1)`: `f(0) = −1 < 0 < 1 = f(1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_B3","kind":"theorem","line":1428,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1428-L1435","doc":"`log B₃ = ½·log t − i·(π − arg a)/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_A3","kind":"theorem","line":1420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1420-L1426","doc":"`log A₃ = ½·log t + i·(π − arg a)/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.three_log_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.three_log_A3","kind":"theorem","line":1404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1404-L1418","doc":"`3·log A₃ + log a = log t + iπ` — Route 61's angle identity, instantiated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.A3_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.A3_alt","kind":"theorem","line":1401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1401-L1402","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.den_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.den_comm","kind":"theorem","line":1399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1399-L1399","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_conj_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_conj_a","kind":"theorem","line":1391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1391-L1397","doc":"`log (conj a) = −½·log t − i·arg a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_t","kind":"theorem","line":1387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1387-L1389","doc":"`log t` is real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_a","kind":"theorem","line":1380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1380-L1385","doc":"`log a = −½·log t + i·arg a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.log_norm","kind":"theorem","line":1373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1373-L1378","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.norm_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.norm_pos","kind":"theorem","line":1371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1371-L1371","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.norm_sq_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.norm_sq_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1367-L1369","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.pentagon_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.pentagon_lower","kind":"theorem","line":1352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1352-L1359","doc":"**The second pentagon instance**, the mirror of `pentagon_upper`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_inv_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_inv_a","kind":"theorem","line":1348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1348-L1350","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.inv_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.inv_B3","kind":"theorem","line":1343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1343-L1346","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mem_conj_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mem_conj_a","kind":"theorem","line":1340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1340-L1341","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.B3_im_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.B3_im_neg","kind":"theorem","line":1336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1336-L1338","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.B3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.B3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1332-L1334","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.B3","kind":"def","line":1328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1328-L1330","doc":"The lower composite argument, `B₃ = conj A₃` — the same expression at the\nconjugate root, since `t` is real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.pentagon_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.pentagon_upper","kind":"theorem","line":1314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1314-L1326","doc":"**The first pentagon instance**, in the capstone's shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_inv_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_inv_conj","kind":"theorem","line":1308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1308-L1312","doc":"`1 − b⁻¹ = 1 − a·t`, since `a·b·t = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.inv_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.inv_A3","kind":"theorem","line":1289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1289-L1306","doc":"`(1−a)/(1−at) = A₃⁻¹` — Route 55's `(1−a)(1−b) = (1−ab)²` with the pair\n`(a, t)` and third root `conj a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mem_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mem_A3","kind":"theorem","line":1286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1286-L1287","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mem_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mem_a","kind":"theorem","line":1284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1284-L1284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.A3_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.A3_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":1276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1276-L1282","doc":"`Im A₃ > 0`: positive real numerator over a denominator below the axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.den_im_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.den_im_neg","kind":"theorem","line":1270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1270-L1274","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.den_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.den_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1263-L1268","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_t_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_t_cast","kind":"theorem","line":1261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1261-L1261","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_t_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_t_pos","kind":"theorem","line":1259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1259-L1259","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.A3","kind":"def","line":1256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1256-L1257","doc":"The upper composite argument `A₃ = (1−t)/(1−a·t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.branch_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.branch_lower","kind":"theorem","line":1234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1234-L1252","doc":"**The branch integer at the lower root is `−1`.** With `branch_upper` and\n`branch_real` this is the full branch datum `ε = (+1, −1, 0)` the corpus records\nfor the 5₂ saddle — **proved**, where it had been measured. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.normSq_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.normSq_mul","kind":"theorem","line":1229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1229-L1232","doc":"`|a|²·t = 1` — the modulus fact, immediate from the norm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.pair_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.pair_rel","kind":"theorem","line":1224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1224-L1227","doc":"The pair relation the angle identity needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.branch_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.branch_upper","kind":"theorem","line":1218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1218-L1222","doc":"**The branch integer at the upper root is `+1`** — the value the corpus\nrecords as `ε₁`, now proved rather than measured. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.branch_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.branch_real","kind":"theorem","line":1213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1213-L1216","doc":"**The branch integer at the real root is `0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.re_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.re_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":1208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1208-L1211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.two_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.two_re","kind":"theorem","line":1201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1201-L1206","doc":"`2·Re a = 2 − t`, from the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.one_sub_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1195-L1199","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1193-L1193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.cubic_conj_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.cubic_conj_a","kind":"theorem","line":1188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1188-L1191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.cubic_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.cubic_a","kind":"theorem","line":1185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1185-L1186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.cubic_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.cubic_t","kind":"theorem","line":1182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1182-L1183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.him","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.him","kind":"theorem","line":1176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1176-L1176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.hprod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.hprod","kind":"theorem","line":1175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1175-L1175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.hp2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.hp2","kind":"theorem","line":1174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1174-L1174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.hsum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.hsum","kind":"theorem","line":1173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1173-L1173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ht1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ht1","kind":"theorem","line":1172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1172-L1172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ht0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.ht0","kind":"theorem","line":1171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1171-L1171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.a","kind":"def","line":1170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1170-L1170","doc":"the root in the upper half plane ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.t","kind":"def","line":1168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1168-L1168","doc":"the real root ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1166-L1166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.SaddleRoots","kind":"structure","line":1163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1163-L1176","doc":"**The 5₂ saddle cubic's roots as data**: a real root `t ∈ (0,1)` and a\nconjugate pair whose upper member is `a`. The three symmetric functions are the\ncubic `X³ − 2X² + 3X − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq_lower","kind":"theorem","line":1132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1132-L1154","doc":"**The branch integer at the lower complex root is `−1`** — the mirror of\n`saddle_branch_eq_upper`, from `Im y < 0` and `Re y ≤ 1`. The expression lies in\n`(−7π/2, 0) ⊂ (−4π, 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq_upper","kind":"theorem","line":1104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1104-L1130","doc":"**The branch integer at the upper complex root is `1`**, from two crude sign\nconditions: `Im y > 0` and `Re y ≤ 1`.\n\nThose give `arg y ∈ (0, π)` and `arg(1−y) ∈ (−π/2, 0)`, so the branch expression\nlies in `(0, 7π/2) ⊂ (0, 4π)` — inside the window, with room. Nothing numeric,\nand no fact about the cubic beyond the cubic itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq_real","kind":"theorem","line":1085,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1085-L1102","doc":"**The branch integer at the real root is `0`** — both arguments vanish, so no\nwindow argument is needed at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_branch_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1067,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1067-L1083","doc":"**The saddle branch equation, integer pinned.**\n\n    2·log y − 3·log(1−y) = 2πi·n\n\nfrom the cubic alone plus a window on `2·arg y − 3·arg(1−y)`. The window has\nwidth `4π`, so the bounds needed are crude: for the real root both arguments\nvanish (`n = 0`); for `y₁` the expression lies in `(0, 7π/2) ⊂ (0, 4π)` from\n`Im y₁ > 0` and `Re y₁ < 1` alone (`n = 1`); for `y₂` it is the mirror\n(`n = −1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_sq_eq_one_sub_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_sq_eq_one_sub_cube","kind":"theorem","line":1060,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1060-L1065","doc":"**`y² = (1−y)³` IS the saddle cubic.** `(1−y)³ − y² = −(y³−2y²+3y−1)`\nidentically, so the multiplicative relation the branch equation needs is the\ncubic itself and nothing extra is assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_clog_cube_of_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_clog_cube_of_roots","kind":"theorem","line":1039,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1039-L1058","doc":"**Link G3's angle identity, with the argument bounds discharged.**\n\n    3·log a₃ + log y₁ = log y₃ + iπ\n\nfrom root data alone — the symmetric functions, the cubic, three non-vanishing\nconditions, the conjugate-pair structure, and two `Im ≥ 0` facts. **No `arg`\nhypothesis survives**, and nothing numeric enters: the only quantitative input is\n`Re a₃ = 1/2`, which is `saddle_argThree_add_eq_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_arg_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_arg_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":1022,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1022-L1037","doc":"**The three sign conditions of link G3, discharged from the root data.**\n\n`Re a₃ = 1/2 > 0` gives `arg a₃ ≤ π/2`; `Im a₃ ≥ 0` and `Im y₁ ≥ 0` give the two\nnon-negativity conditions. Nothing numeric is needed — the only quantitative\ninput is that `Re a₃` is exactly `1/2`, which is `saddle_argThree_add_eq_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.re_eq_half_of_add_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.re_eq_half_of_add_conj","kind":"theorem","line":1014,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L1014-L1020","doc":"`z.re = 1/2` from `z + conj z = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_argThree_add_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_argThree_add_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":999,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L999-L1012","doc":"**`a₃` and its partner sum to `1`.**\n\n    (1−c)/(1−ca) + (1−c)/(1−cb) = 1\n\nfor the three roots. With `b = conj a` and `c` real this says `Re a₃ = 1/2`,\nwhich is the one sign condition of link G3 with any content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.one_sub_mul_third","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.one_sub_mul_third","kind":"theorem","line":993,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L993-L997","doc":"`1 − cb = (a−1)/a`, since `cb = 1/a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_pair_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_pair_rel","kind":"theorem","line":987,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L987-L991","doc":"The pair relation `a²c + ac² − 2ac + 1 = 0` — \"the third root is `1/(ac)` and\nthe three sum to `2`\" — from the symmetric functions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_clog_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_clog_cube","kind":"theorem","line":953,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L953-L978","doc":"**Link G3's branch pinning, assembled.** `saddle_arg_cube'` gives\n`a₃³·y₁ = −y₃`; `MathlibExt.clog_cube_mul` turns that into\n\n    3·log a₃ + log y₁ = log y₃ + iπ\n\nwith **no** branch correction, given only three crude sign conditions on the\narguments. Those three are what remains of Route 58's link G3 — facts about the\nspecific algebraic numbers (`Re a₃ = 1/2 > 0`, `Im a₃ > 0`, `Im y₁ > 0`), not\nabout dilogarithms.\n\n⚠ Stated with the sign conditions as hypotheses. They are **not** discharged\nhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_arg_cube'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_arg_cube'","kind":"theorem","line":944,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L944-L951","doc":"The same in the form the pentagon uses: the cube of the composite argument\ntimes the other root is minus the real root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_arg_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_arg_cube","kind":"theorem","line":928,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L928-L942","doc":"**The angle identity's algebraic core.** For two roots `a`, `c` of the saddle\ncubic (`hR` says the third root is `1/(ac)`),\n\n    ((1−c)/(1−ca))³ · a = −c\n\ni.e. `a₃³·y₁ = −y₃`. Taking arguments gives `3·arg a₃ + arg y₁ = π`, which is the\nangle identity `arg a₃ = (π − arg y₁)/3` that Route 58's inversion evaluation\nrests on. The identity is *not* a consequence of `hR` alone — the cubic is needed\ntoo, and the cofactors below are what a Gröbner reduction against both returns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagon_arg_reciprocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagon_arg_reciprocal","kind":"theorem","line":913,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L913-L926","doc":"**The two composite pentagon arguments at the saddle are reciprocal.**\n\n`a₅ = 1/a₃`, i.e. `(1−a)(1−b) = (1−ab)²`, for any two roots `a, b` of the saddle\ncubic — and the identity *is* the cubic, satisfied by the third root `c`. This is\nwhy the degree-6 elements `a₃, a₅` drop out of the relation: `L(a₃) + L(1/a₃)` is\nelementary by inversion, leaving only the degree-3 orbit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_of_plastic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_of_plastic","kind":"theorem","line":906,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L906-L911","doc":"The inverse transport: a root of `X³ − X + 1` maps back under `x ↦ 1/(1−x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.plastic_of_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.plastic_of_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":900,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L900-L904","doc":"A root of the saddle cubic maps to a root of `X³ − X + 1`, whose roots are\nthe negatives of the plastic numbers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_to_plastic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_to_plastic","kind":"theorem","line":892,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L892-L898","doc":"**The 5₂ saddle cubic is the plastic cubic, transported by `y ↦ 1 − 1/y`.**\n\nAn identity of rational functions — nothing is reduced modulo the cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_pi_sq_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_pi_sq_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":844,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L844-L859","doc":"**The complex five-term identity, unconditionally, in one variable.**\n\n    L(a) + L(w) + L((1−a)/(1−aw)) + L(1−aw) + L((1−w)/(1−aw)) = π²/2\n\nfor `L = cRogersL`, every real `a ∈ (0,1)` and **every** `w` off both real cuts —\n`w` complex, `|w|` arbitrarily large, either side of either cut.\n\n⚠ One variable. With both variables non-real it is false; see the section\nheader. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonRegular_of_mem_rogersDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonRegular_of_mem_rogersDomain","kind":"theorem","line":805,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L805-L842","doc":"**Every point of `rogersDomain` is regular, against a real `a ∈ (0,1)`.**\n\nTwo cases, and neither is delicate: `Im w ≠ 0` propagates to all four arguments,\nand `Im w = 0` puts `w` in `(0,1)` where `PentagonRegular.of_real` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.isPreconnected_rogersDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.isPreconnected_rogersDomain","kind":"theorem","line":792,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L792-L803","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.rogersDomain_eq_union","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.rogersDomain_eq_union","kind":"theorem","line":770,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L770-L790","doc":"`rogersDomain` is the union of two convex-joined pieces: each half-plane\nglued to the strip `0 < re < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.im_div_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.im_div_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":764,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L764-L768","doc":"`Im(p/q) ≠ 0` from the numerator of `Complex.div_im`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.mem_rogersDomain_of_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.mem_rogersDomain_of_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":760,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L760-L762","doc":"Non-zero imaginary part puts a point off both cuts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum_snd_of_region","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum_snd_of_region","kind":"theorem","line":716,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L716-L725","doc":"Transport in `y`, for free from the symmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_swap","kind":"theorem","line":713,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L713-L714","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_symm","kind":"theorem","line":708,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L708-L711","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_pi_sq_div_two_of_region","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_pi_sq_div_two_of_region","kind":"theorem","line":674,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L674-L697","doc":"**A complex five-term identity — conditional on the region.**\n\nOn any open connected set `S` of `x` that stays `PentagonRegular` for a real\n`y ∈ (0,1)` and contains a real point of `(0,1)`,\n\n    L(x) + L(y) + L((1−x)/(1−xy)) + L(1−xy) + L((1−y)/(1−xy)) = π²/2\n\nfor the complex Rogers dilogarithm `L = cRogersL`, at **every** point of `S` —\nincluding points where nothing is real.\n\n⚠ The hypothesis `hreg` is the entire remaining difficulty, and it is not a\ntechnicality: a regular region reaching the real square *forces* the naive log\nexpansions, so where the flattening is non-trivial no such region can exist.\nThat is the obstruction and the missing region seen twice.\n\n**The 5₂ sum rule is PROVED**: `FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule`\nand `fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds`, sorry-free, standard axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L656-L672","doc":"**The constant, as a number.** On the positive real square the complex\npentagon sum is `π²/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.rogersL_pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.rogersL_pentagon","kind":"theorem","line":630,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L630-L654","doc":"**The real pentagon sum is `π²/2`.**\n\nAbel's relation gives the sum over `x, y, xy, x(1−y)/(1−xy), y(1−x)/(1−xy)`;\nreflection turns the last three into the pentagon's `1−xy`, `(1−x)/(1−xy)`,\n`(1−y)/(1−xy)`, at the cost of `3 · π²/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cRogersL_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":617,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L617-L628","doc":"**`cRogersL` is the corpus's real Rogers dilogarithm on `(0,1)`.**\n\nThis is the bridge the lane was missing between the complex pentagon and the\nreal five-term identity that was already proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cLiTwoExt_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cLiTwoExt_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":612,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L612-L615","doc":"`cLiTwoExt` at a real point of `(−1,1)` is the corpus's real `LiTwo`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cLiTwo_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.cLiTwo_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":603,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L603-L610","doc":"The complex `Li₂` series at a real argument is the real one — same series,\ntermwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_of_region_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_of_region_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":560,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L560-L581","doc":"**The statement the 5₂ lane actually wants, with its one remaining input\nnamed.** Give an open connected set of `x` on which the pentagon stays regular\nand which contains a real point of `(0,1)`, and the complex five-term sum is\nconstant on it — equal to the value it has on the real square, where the real\nfive-term identity already pins it.\n\nThe hypothesis `hreg` was the whole difficulty when this was written. It is\ndischarged below: `pentagonRegular_of_mem_rogersDomain` supplies the regularity\nand `isPreconnected_rogersDomain` the connectedness, so `rogersDomain` **is**\nsuch a set — which is what turns this conditional statement into the\nunconditional `pentagonSum_eq_pi_sq_div_two`.\n\n**The 5₂ sum rule is PROVED**:\n`QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule`\nand `fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds`, sorry-free, standard axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defects_eq_zero_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defects_eq_zero_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L548-L558","doc":"**A real base point supplies all five base values.** `0 < x₀, y < 1` makes\nevery defect vanish, by `pentagon_branch_conditions_of_real`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_of_region","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum_eq_of_region","kind":"theorem","line":530,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L530-L546","doc":"**The complex pentagon sum is constant on such a region.**\n\nThis is as far as the derivative argument reaches. What it still does not give is\na *region*: for the 5₂ saddle values `y₁, y₂` none is exhibited, and exhibiting\none is exactly where flattening — Neumann's `ker ν` — can obstruct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum_of_region","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum_of_region","kind":"theorem","line":497,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L497-L528","doc":"**The pentagon's derivative vanishes throughout a regular region that reaches\na point where the branch conditions hold.**\n\nNo branch condition is assumed at `x` itself — only at the base point `x₀`, and\nthey are *transported* by `eq_zero_of_hasDerivAt_zero`. This is what the phrase\n\"continue the branch conditions\" reduces to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectFive'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectFive'","kind":"theorem","line":474,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L474-L491","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectFive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectFive","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L462-L472","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectFour'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectFour'","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L448-L460","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectThree'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectThree'","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L429-L446","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectThree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_defectThree","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L416-L427","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_clog_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_clog_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L409-L414","doc":"`d/dw log(1−wy) = (1−xy)⁻¹·(−y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_clog_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_clog_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L400-L407","doc":"`d/dw log(1−w) = −(1−x)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectFive'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectFive'","kind":"def","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L391-L394","doc":"`log(1−a₅) − log y − log(1−w) + log(1−wy)`; the branch condition `e5'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectFive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectFive","kind":"def","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L387-L389","doc":"`log a₅ − log(1−y) + log(1−wy)`; the branch condition `e5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectFour'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectFour'","kind":"def","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L383-L385","doc":"`log(wy) − log w − log y`; the branch condition `e4'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectThree'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectThree'","kind":"def","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L378-L381","doc":"`log(1−a₃) − log w − log(1−y) + log(1−wy)`; the branch condition `e3'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectThree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.defectThree","kind":"def","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L374-L376","doc":"`log a₃ − log(1−w) + log(1−wy)`; the branch condition `e3` is its vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.eq_zero_of_hasDerivAt_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.eq_zero_of_hasDerivAt_zero","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L361-L370","doc":"**The propagation principle.** A defect that is holomorphic with vanishing\nderivative on an open connected set and vanishes somewhere on it vanishes\neverywhere on it. This is what turns a branch condition checked at one point into\none that holds on a whole region. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.of_real","kind":"theorem","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L346-L357","doc":"On the positive real square, every point is regular. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.one_sub_y_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.one_sub_y_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L343-L344","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.y_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.y_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L340-L341","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.mul_ne_zero'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.mul_ne_zero'","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L336-L338","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.den_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.den_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L333-L334","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.one_sub_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.one_sub_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L330-L331","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular.ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L328-L328","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.PentagonRegular","kind":"def","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L316-L322","doc":"The pentagon's analytic side conditions at `w`, for a fixed `y`: all four\n`x`-dependent arguments avoid both real cuts. Everything else the pentagon needs\n— `w ≠ 0`, `1−w ≠ 0`, `y ≠ 0`, `1−y ≠ 0`, `1−wy ≠ 0`, and slit-plane membership\nfor each logarithm — is a consequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L271-L290","doc":"**`hasDerivAt_pentagonSum` instantiated: every hypothesis discharged.**\n\nNo branch condition survives as a hypothesis, so the theorem above is not\nvacuous. It is *only* that — the region is the one where the real five-term\nidentity was already available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagon_branch_conditions_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagon_branch_conditions_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L199-L269","doc":"**The five branch conditions hold on the positive real square.**\n\nEach side is the cast of a real logarithm of a positive real, so the expansions\nare `Real.log_mul` and `Real.log_div` and no branch is chosen. This is what makes\n`hasDerivAt_pentagonSum` non-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagon_args_mem_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagon_args_mem_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L187-L197","doc":"The pentagon's arguments, as reals in `(0,1)`, on the positive real square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_pentagonSum","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L92-L168","doc":"**The complex pentagon's `x`-derivative vanishes.**\n\nThe analytic content of §7h. The four `rogersDomain` hypotheses are what makes\neach term differentiable; the five `e…` hypotheses are the branch conditions,\nand they are exactly the unproved input — see\n`pentagon_branch_conditions_of_real` for a region where they hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.pentagonSum","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L87-L90","doc":"The five-term sum, as a function of the differentiation variable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_argFive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_argFive","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L77-L83","doc":"`a₅(w) = (1−y)/(1−wy)`, derivative `(1−y)·y/(1−xy)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_argThree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_argThree","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L67-L75","doc":"`a₃(w) = (1−w)/(1−wy)`, derivative `(y−1)/(1−xy)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_argFour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.hasDerivAt_argFour","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoComplexPentagon.lean#L62-L65","doc":"`a₄(w) = 1 − wy`, derivative `−y`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}